   the 63 matched cases: the entry 55 of 63, always robust 49 of 63 (non-robust cases 14); non-robust calls 14: right 10, wrong 4; robust calls on non-robust cases 4 (both wrong); discordant 10 against 4; exact two-sided McNemar p = 0.1796 (0.18); Clopper-Pearson 95% interval of the entry 0.765 to 0.944 (0.77 to 0.94); always robust 0.778
   the 22 newer (AIME-2026) cases among them: the entry 17 of 22, always robust 12 of 22 (non-robust cases 10); non-robust calls 9: right 7, wrong 2; robust calls on non-robust cases 3 (both wrong); discordant 7 against 2; exact two-sided McNemar p = 0.1797 (0.18); Clopper-Pearson 95% interval of the entry 0.546 to 0.922 (0.55 to 0.92); always robust 0.545

## 2. boards (totals only; hidden labels are never read): the smallest two-sided sign-test p a total allows
   a total k against always robust's r needs at least d = k - r non-robust calls; at best all d are right and no other non-robust call is made, so p >= 2 x 0.5^d (exact two-sided sign test on the discordant cases, capped at 1)
   main board, the entry (15 of 21): always robust 10; gain +5; smallest p 0.0625 (0.062); never <= 0.05
   small board, the entry (9 of 14): always robust 7; gain +2; smallest p 0.5000 (0.500); never <= 0.05
   main board, earlier build (16 of 21): always robust 10; gain +6; smallest p 0.0312 (0.031); p <= 0.05 only if the entry made at most 6 non-robust calls
   main board, earlier build (17 of 21): always robust 10; gain +7; smallest p 0.0156 (0.016); p <= 0.05 only if the entry made at most 9 non-robust calls
   small board, earlier build (10 of 14): always robust 7; gain +3; smallest p 0.2500 (0.250); never <= 0.05

